ite(p)\nE\ncd .. && python3 run_tests.py | tail -3"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":8,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"All 6 tests in `run_tests.py` now pass. I fixed these bugs:\n\n1. **`parse_date` (`parse.py`)**: it returned `(year, day, month)`. It now returns `(year, month, day)`. This also fixed `parse_record`.\n2. **`top_items` (`report.py`)**: it sorted by total ascending. It now sorts by total descending, with ties broken by item name ascending, as the docstring says. `summary_line` uses it, so that is fixed too.\n3. **`format_cents` (`money.py`)**: negative amounts were formatted wrongly because floor division and modulo on a negative number give odd results. For example, -5 cents came out as `-$-1.95` instead of `-$0.05`. It now formats the absolute value and adds the sign afterwards.\n4. **`parse_amount` (`money.py`)**: I also made it tolerate whitespace between the minus sign and the `$`, as in `- $3.10`. This is a small robustness change, and the visible tests don't depend on it.\n\nI haven't tested negative amounts in `format_cents` beyond the visible test (`-310`).","ttft_ms":1725,"type":"result","duration_ms":16463,"uuid":"20a307a7-620f-400e-b0ef-faef6e21e4c0","ttft_stream_ms":1048,"time_to_request_ms":26,"first_content_frame_ms":1048,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
